WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
Welcome to RehearsAI for Android and iPhone.
In this video, you'll learn how actors and team

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.240
members join a shared project, rehearse 
their roles anywhere, record dialogue,

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.480
and collaborate with the rest of the cast.
While the Windows version is designed for

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.280
creating and managing projects, the mobile 
app is built for rehearsing, recording,

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.000
and participating in those projects.
Let's get started.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.920
To join a rehearsal project,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.720
tap Join Project and enter the project code 
provided by your director or project owner.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.640
After joining, you'll see 
the available characters.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:41.840
Simply select your assigned role, and the 
project will be downloaded to your device.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.960
The project owner has full editing privileges.
Project members cannot edit the script,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.360
rename characters, or modify the project 
structure. This ensures that everyone rehearses

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:57.640
using the same approved version of the script.
As a project member, your role is to rehearse,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.120
record your dialogue, and synchronize your 
recordings with the shared project.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:10.600
You can begin rehearsing immediately—even if other 
cast members haven't recorded their lines yet.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.720
For any character without a recording,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.840
you can assign an AI voice to perform 
that role during rehearsal.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:22.560
As other actors upload their real recordings, 
those recordings automatically become available,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.360
allowing you to rehearse with the actual voices 
of your cast instead of AI-generated ones.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.160
This provides a smooth transition from early 
preparation to full cast rehearsals.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.840
Open your assigned character and record 
each dialogue line individually.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.640
Recording line by line makes it easy to improve 
your performance and re-record only the lines

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.840
that need adjustment.
Once you're satisfied,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.760
upload your recordings to the shared project so 
they're available to the rest of the cast.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:06.320
RehearsAI gives you flexible rehearsal controls.
Choose the character you want to practice,

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:12.120
then customize how the dialogue is displayed.
You can show or hide your own lines, display

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:17.640
the previous sentence, the next sentence, or 
both, depending on how you prefer to rehearse.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.160
These options help you focus on memorization, 
timing, and responding naturally to

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.840
surrounding dialogue.
 
For large productions,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.840
the project owner can organize the 
script into individual scenes.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:36.360
Instead of navigating the entire script, you can 
simply select the scene you want to practice.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:41.840
This allows you to rehearse or record only 
the scenes relevant to your upcoming rehearsal

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.280
or performance, making preparation 
faster and much more organized.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.866
you can download recordings from other cast members once they have finished their recordings

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.880
Whenever the project owner updates the project 
in the Windows application, you can synchronize

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.271
your device to receive the latest changes.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.680
If a dialogue line is removed from the project,

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:15.560
its associated recording is automatically removed 
from every device connected to that project.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:20.880
If a dialogue line is modified, the 
corresponding recording is marked with a warning,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.600
indicating that it should be recorded 
again to match the updated script.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.200
RehearsAI also makes it easy to revisit 
productions months or even years later.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.960
Since the complete project—including 
dialogue, character assignments, scenes,

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:44.320
and recordings—is securely stored, the cast 
can resume rehearsals without rebuilding

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:48.520
the project or starting from scratch.
This is especially valuable for theatre

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.320
productions that return for future 
performances or touring shows.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:57.240
RehearsAI for Android and iPhone allows 
actors to rehearse anytime and anywhere

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:02.120
while staying connected to the entire cast.
Whether you're practicing with AI voices during

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:06.480
the early stages or with recordings from 
your fellow actors later in production,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.560
RehearsAI provides a flexible and 
efficient rehearsal experience.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:18.600
going with synchronized projects, scene-based 
organization, real voice recordings, and

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:25.440
intelligent collaboration tools, your entire cast 
stays connected and ready for every rehearsal.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.760
Thank you for watching, and 
see you in the next tutorial.
